.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt PROC_WAIT 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm proc_wait
.Nd wait for a process to become terminal and read its exit code
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Ft int
.Fn proc_wait "Handle proc" "int *out_code"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
system call blocks until
.Fa proc
is terminal and stores its exit code in
.Fa out_code .
The code is the one published by
.Xr exit 2 ,
.Xr thread_exit 2
of the last thread, or
.Xr proc_terminate 2 .
.Pp
A process created with
.Xr proc_create 2
but never given a thread is reaped at once: it can never run, so
.Nm
completes immediately.
.Pp
.Nm
may be called again on the same terminal process; it returns the stored code each time.  The
teardown itself (address space, handle table, scheme names) runs exactly once.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
On success
.Nm
returns a non-negative value; on failure it returns a negative error number.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Er EBADF
.Fa proc
is not a process handle.
.It Er EFAULT
.Fa out_code
is not writable user memory.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr exit 2 ,
.Xr proc_create 2 ,
.Xr proc_terminate 2 ,
.Xr thread_exit 2
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
